[h1]Sea Power Radio[/h1]
The radio net sounds like people instead of a screen reader – and your units tell you [b]why[/b] they aren't doing what you ordered.

[list]
[*][b]A voice for every unit[/b] – every ship, aircraft and helicopter of yours, including everything your carriers and airbases can launch, gets its own voice and a NATO callsign for the mission ("Viper two-one", "Sentinel"). 43 distinct voices, the same ones again when you reload.
[*][b]Stock voice lines replaced[/b] – re-spoken by the unit that actually said them, through a radio filter with hiss, clicks and squelch.
[*][b]Brevity on the net[/b] – a unit only gives its callsign when it takes over the net; a wingman just says "two, fox three".
[*][b]Why not?[/b] – "Negative, target not in rear aspect", "Unable, holding formation on lead", reload times, sonar-only contacts – spoken, on screen and in the log. Order queue window (F8) with the selected unit's stacked attack orders.
[*][b]No contact spam[/b] – lost / regained / intermittent contacts with sensible delays; track numbers in messages are clickable.
[*][b]Everything clickable[/b] – every unit and track a message mentions takes the camera there.
[*][b]Fuel calls[/b] – joker, bingo and fuel emergency against the nearest deck or airfield that can take the aircraft.
[*][b]RTB at a glance[/b] – aircraft heading home are yellow on the map and in the formation manager.
[*][b]Search and rescue calls[/b] – survivors in the water, rescuer on the way, souls aboard, cabin full, delivered on deck.
[*][b]Unit roles[/b] in the formation manager – Destroyer, Attack Submarine, CAP, Strike, ASW Helicopter… in your game language.
[/list]

All voices are pre-rendered – nothing is generated while you play, no internet needed. About 390 MB.

[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[b]Anchor Chain[/b] is required: [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3380210757]subscribe[/url] and follow its [url=https://seapower-modders.github.io/AnchorChain/install-anchor-chain.html]installation guide[/url] (one manual step: copy its preloader into the game folder).

[h2]Settings[/h2]
[i]<Sea Power>\BepInEx\config\dev.sewerlabs.seapowerradio.cfg[/i] – volumes, radio noise, which calls are spoken (contact reports, fuel, SAR, refusals), the order queue key, unit roles, logging.

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
Sea Power 0.8.x. If a game update moves something the mod needs, only that feature switches off and the log says which. Works together with Topographic Map and Pop-Out Windows. No game files are changed.

[h2]Problems?[/h2]
Please post the file [i]<Sea Power>\BepInEx\LogOutput.log[/i] with your report.

[h2]Credits[/h2]
Voices generated with Chatterbox (Resemble AI), cloned from speakers of the CSTR VCTK Corpus – Yamagishi, Veaux, MacDonald (2019), University of Edinburgh, The Centre for Speech Technology Research, [url=https://doi.org/10.7488/ds/2645]doi.org/10.7488/ds/2645[/url], licensed [url=https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/]CC BY 4.0[/url]. The voice clips are CC BY 4.0 as well. Built on BepInEx, HarmonyX and Anchor Chain.

Source code (MIT): [url=https://github.com/struckl/SeaPowerRadio]github.com/struckl/SeaPowerRadio[/url]
